 ## 2026-07-20
 
+### 2158 — Shared relay hostile corpus is semantically identical in Swift and Go (TASK-260715-297gq6)
+- IMPLEMENTATION: Both protocol bindings consume the checked `lcg64-v1` regression corpus. Four fixed 64-bit seeds drive 2,096 deterministic cases across both envelope directions, legal and mutated frames, hostile declared lengths, arbitrary chunking/coalescing, inner HEV parsing, EOF, cancellation, and reset. Each language derives the same four stable semantic digests, so code/phase/scope/disposition or ordering drift fails the common gate without comparing implementation-specific error text.
+- REVIEW REWORK: Decoder metrics now count internal byte/prefix/header/frame processing iterations and current/peak body-allocation bytes. Shared prefix-only cases declare exactly 4,096 bytes and 4,097 bytes, proving the accepted ceiling allocates at most 4,096 bytes and the next value allocates zero. The deterministic work ceiling is `inputBytes + 3 × bodyAllocations + 1`.
+- BOUNDS: Swift and Go report the same 28,577 consumed bytes, 20-byte peak retained state, 4,096-byte peak allocated body, two maximum body allocations per case, 42 maximum processing iterations against a 43-iteration maximum ceiling, five maximum chunks, 96-byte diagnostics, and zero retained/outstanding body bytes after every terminal and reset path. Successful output records each exact seed ID, value, and semantic digest without payload content.
+- VERIFICATION: `make relay-protocol-check`, Go checkptr, Swift AddressSanitizer, strict Swift format, gofmt, Go vet, shell syntax, JSON validation, diff validation, and board validation pass. A five-second native Go fuzz run passed 1,453,381 executions with 19 new coverage-interesting inputs and no crash/invariant failure. Protocol source coverage is Swift 93.21% (1,797/1,928 lines) and Go 85.7% statements.
+- TOOLCHAIN: The repository still lacks the authoritative `relay/go.mod` and pinned Go 1.26.5 owned by TASK-260715-27uz4n, so local Go evidence uses the accepted standard-library-only `CGO_ENABLED=0` smoke under Go 1.25.5. This does not substitute for the later release-toolchain gate.
+
 ### 2118 — Canonical relay v1 vectors use an independent deterministic oracle (TASK-260715-1q7u14)
 - IMPLEMENTATION: A Python-standard-library reference path now emits and independently parses 89 canonical vectors covering both hello directions, all six message types and legal directions, all three HEV address types, every hello status and UDP error code, fixed and negotiated boundaries, malformed fields, association/session failure dispositions, and fragmented/coalesced stream plans. Limit metadata names generated schema selectors instead of copying policy values.
 - PRIVACY: Corpus endpoints use RFC documentation ranges, `.example`, and one opaque `x` byte for the required minimum-domain boundary; payloads use a fixed public byte pattern. Strict Swift and Go loaders reject unknown schema keys, validate IDs/chunks/provenance/schema digest/coverage, and report only the exact stable vector ID plus a finite local reason on failure.
